    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Menomonie-WI/Adjunct-Instructor-Pool---Online-Professional-Development-Education--OPDE-_JR10008701": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor Pool – Online Professional Development for Educators (OPDE)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Adjunct Instructor Pool – Online Professional Development for Educators (OPDE) Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Each department at the University of Wisconsin – Stout   can   maintain   an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair.   The instructor   is responsible for   teaching   courses as   assigned .    T eaching involves   preparing for and holding classes in the modality assigned,   maintaining   currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students’ work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work,   maintaining   appropriate records , and holding office hours.   Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean.   Department and/or College Description   The  OPDE program is a collaboration between the Teaching, Learning, and Leadership Department and Stout Online at UW-Stout. The OPDE program offers   fully online , graduate level professional development courses and certificate programs designed for working adults and educators   seeking   to advance their careers in areas such as Instructional Design, Mathematics Instruction, and Reading Instruction. Many OPDE courses can be applied towards teaching license renewal or used as electives for UW-Stout degree programs. The OPDE program’s curriculum is designed and taught by experienced practitioners and instructors at UW-Stout, and across the country.   For a full listing of   OPDE courses, please see   our   website .   UW-Stout’s OPDE program is committed to creating an inclusive, accessible, and supportive online learning environment for all students. Candidates with experience working collaboratively with diverse groups and   individuals and   who can contribute to inclusive and   equitable   online learning practices are encouraged to   identify   their experience in these areas.   Qualifications   Minimal/Required Qualifications:    Doctorate   in relevant field of   course(s)   or   M aster’s Degree   in relevant field + 5 years of relevant professional experience   Professional experience in areas of expertise (Instructional Design, Mathematics   Specialist , Reading   Teacher, Reading Specialist , etc.)       Preferred Qualifications:   Demonstrated experience teaching or   facilitating   online courses for adult learners    Proficiency   in online learning management systems (Canvas, etc.)   Proficiency   in Microsoft Office applications   Strong written and interpersonal skills   Fluency in oral and written English communication     Required Application Materials:   Cover letter*   Resume/CV   * Please use your cover letter to describe your teaching specialty ,   relevant areas of expertise , and teaching interests .   Contact   for questions:   Kathryn Hamilton, Interim OPDE Coordinator   Email:   hamiltonk@uwstout.edu     Phone: (715) 232-2442     Note:   The pool of applications is reviewed as opportunities become available throughout the year.   This is an open pool for candidates to apply. If the department has an opening and is interested in learning more about your qualifications, you will be contacted. Thank   you sincerely   for your time.   The University of Wisconsin-Stout does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. A successful applicant will be responsible for ensuring eligibility for employment in the United States on or before the effective date of the appointment and for maintaining work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact our Human Resources office, Phone: 715.232.2149. Guidelines to ensure consideration:     Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required application materials.      Within your cover letter address each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications specified for this position. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement.   It is the policy of UW-Stout to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact us using the information below. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodation for a qualified individual's disability.    The Universities of Wisconsin provides an excellent benefits package including participation in the Wisconsin State retirement plan, demonstrating our commitment to the diverse needs of our employees.  Employee Benefits:  https://www.wisconsin.edu/ohrwd/benefits/ To calculate the estimated value of your total compensation, use the Health & Retirement Contributions Estimator | Employee Benefits (wisconsin.edu) Employment is contingent upon the final candidate’s completing a criminal background check and being cleared to work by the Human Resources Office.  Employment is also contingent upon the final candidate passing reference checks and an essential job function test, as applicable. The reference check process includes asking the final candidates’ professional references questions regarding employee misconduct, sexual violence, and sexual harassment. Reference checks must be conducted at a minimum with three professional references, at least one of which must be a prior supervisor. Final candidates with previous employment within the Universities of Wisconsin and State of WI agencies will be subject to additional reference checks.  In response to a public records request, the Universities of Wisconsin will not reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in their online application, except that the identity of the successful final candidate will be released. See Wis. Stat. sec. 19.36(7). UW-Stout is committed to providing safety and security of all members of our community in accordance with the Clery Act. For campus safety information and crime statistics visit: https://www.uwstout.edu/life-stout/police-and-parking/clery-information UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Menomonie-WI/Custodian---Facilities-Management-Continuous-Pool_JR10005489": {
      "title": "Custodian - Facilities Management Continuous Pool",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-10-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Custodian - Facilities Management Continuous Pool Job Category: University Staff Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Custodian Job Duties: Key Job Responsibilities: Documents and reports repairs, violations, and pest control needs Utilizes basic equipment and supplies to clean assigned facility areas and remove waste and recyclables Maintains clean and clear walkways to ensure they are free of debris, litter, snow, and ice Monitors and secures facility interior and exterior entrances and reports issues to appropriate entities Maintains organization of supply areas and equipment, documents inventory, and requests additional supplies as needed CUSTODIAN – ACADEMIC BUILDINGS CONTINUOUS RECRUITMENT A BOUT THE JOB:  CUSTODIAN The UW-Stout Academic Custodial Team works to give students, staff, and visitors a great experience by keeping campus buildings clean and well-maintained. Custodial work follows best practices, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), and Work Instructions (WIs). This position reports to the Custodial Supervisor and receives guidance and feedback from Custodial Leads and the Supervisor.  Typical shifts are: 1st Shift: 5:00 a.m. to 1:30 p.m. 2nd Shift: 2:30 p.m. to 11:00 p.m. Depending on the shift, night and weekend differential pay may apply to a position. Night Differential (80 cents) - additional pay for all hours worked on a regularly scheduled shift during the period between 6:00 p.m. and 6:00 a.m. Weekend Differential (80 cents) - additional pay for all hours worked between 12:01 a.m. on Saturday and 12:00 Midnight Sunday Core Job Responsibilities Clean and maintain assigned areas following Stout Cleaning Standards and schedules  Learn and perform all processes and procedures for Restorative cleaning in your area  Use, clean, and care for custodial equipment properly  Keep supply areas and equipment organized  Keep walkways clear of trash, snow, and ice  Track supplies and request more to keep proper inventory levels  Report vandalism, pest issues, and items in need of repair, Monitors and secures facility interior and exterior entrances and reports issues to appropriate entities Work as a team with campus staff, co-workers, and supervisors  Follow safety rules and use Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)  Follow SOPs and WIs for all tasks  Provide quality service by working directly with students, staff, and visitors  Be a helpful point of contact in the building  Wear provided Facilities apparel and ID badge properly  Perform other duties as assigned  Knowledge/Skills and Abilities Minimum Able to read English, speak, and talk with the public.  Able to see clearly enough to read labels and identify objects up to 20 feet away in daylight.  Willing to learn how to use cleaning products safely and correctly  Willing to learn how to use, clean, and care for custodial equipment  Willing to follow UW System, campus, and department work rules  Willing to learn basic computer skills to fill out forms, read messages, and reply to emails  Willing to carry and communicate using a company issued cell phone  Open to giving and receiving feedback in a respectful and professional way  Physical Demands: Daily Tasks:  Walking on flat and uneven surfaces  Standing, stooping, reaching, grasping, pushing, pulling  Using spray bottles, mops, and other hand tools  Reaching and wiping horizontal and vertical surfaces  Sweeping, mopping, and vacuuming  Regular Tasks:  Climbing ladders to reach 10’ ceiling to clean and/or change light bulbs  Lifting or moving up to 50 lbs. alone or more with a team  Kneeling and standing to clean or fix equipment  Working outside in all Wisconsin seasons Preferred Proven success using the Custodial Services Skills listed below  Custodial Services Skills (Required for All Custodial Staff)  Customer Service (Building Relationships)  Works alone and with others to meet cleaning goals. Responds quickly and respectfully. Communicates clearly and kindly with people from different backgrounds.  Thinking and Learning Skills  Uses tools like email, online forms, and SharePoint. Understands information, sees connections, and uses knowledge to improve work.  Personal Responsibility  Takes responsibility for actions. Brings a positive attitude. Accepts feedback, listens, and asks questions when unsure.  Job Knowledge and Problem Solving Uses job skills to complete tasks. Thinks through problems, understands rules and different views, and makes smart choices. Acts professionally.  Leadership  Meets goals, plans ahead, makes decisions, and supports others in a respectful and encouraging way.  Special Requirements Before Employment  Must pass an Essential Job Function test (provided by employer)  Must successfully complete a background check  Must complete UW System Misconduct Reference Check Questions  TO APPLY Go to: https://www.uwstout.edu/about-us/careers-jobs Applicants will need to complete all required fields and attach all required documents prior to submitting the online application. Required application materials : Resume This is a continual recruitment pool.  As positions become available, applications will be screened. **All final candidates will be asked to provide names, email contact information, and/or phone numbers for three (3) references, with at least one being from a manager or supervisor, during the interview process.    It is the policy of UW-Stout to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact us using the information below. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodation for a qualified individual's disability. If you need assistance with the online application process or if you submitted your application prior to uploading all of the required application materials, please contact: Alexandra Bates Phone: 715-232-2438 Email:  batesa@uwstout.edu For job specific questions, please contact: Bradley M. Kupczak Phone: 715-232-2575 Email: kupczakb@uwstout.edu ADDITIONAL INFORMATION The minimum hourly rate for this position is $15.00/hour.  A six-month probationary period is required. Guidelines to ensure consideration:     Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required application materials.      Within your cover letter address each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications specified for this position. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement.   It is the policy of UW-Stout to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact us using the information below. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodation for a qualified individual's disability.    The Universities of Wisconsin provides an excellent benefits package including participation in the Wisconsin State retirement plan, demonstrating our commitment to the diverse needs of our employees.  Employee Benefits:  https://www.wisconsin.edu/ohrwd/benefits/ To calculate the estimated value of your total compensation, use the Health & Retirement Contributions Estimator | Employee Benefits (wisconsin.edu) Employment is contingent upon the final candidate’s completing a criminal background check and being cleared to work by the Human Resources Office.  Employment is also contingent upon the final candidate passing reference checks and an essential job function test, as applicable. The reference check process includes asking the final candidates’ professional references questions regarding employee misconduct, sexual violence, and sexual harassment. Reference checks must be conducted at a minimum with three professional references, at least one of which must be a prior supervisor. Final candidates with previous employment within the Universities of Wisconsin and State of WI agencies will be subject to additional reference checks.  In response to a public records request, the Universities of Wisconsin will not reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in their online application, except that the identity of the successful final candidate will be released. See Wis. Stat. sec. 19.36(7). UW-Stout is committed to providing safety and security of all members of our community in accordance with the Clery Act. For campus safety information and crime statistics visit: https://www.uwstout.edu/life-stout/police-and-parking/clery-information UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."
    }
  },
